sic]  back in his home village he calls the  people for a general talk on hygiene  [Music]  it is 60 miles by river past many rapids  to the regional hospital at puerto  acucho  only the worst cases of emergency are  taken there  the child needing a blood transfusion  the baby who has been born months  premature  iran is a final example of these trends  in health care  it has 12 000 doctors but half of them  practice in the capital tehran  and most of the rest work in other big  towns  [Music]  yet 20 million people still live in  rugged countryside  and there are some 20 000 villages of  less than 100 population  [Music]  how can a country provide an effective  system of health care  for these small scattered communities dr  hussein ronaghi of pallava university  had a plan in 1972 for a new level of  health worker  we thought that we can do  some of the primary health work  by the villagers themselves train them  in the village and deploy them  in the village working as a health  worker  this was an experimental program  something similar to barefoot doctors of  china  but in different socioeconomic  and political situation such as iran  [Music]  what are the health needs of iran what  are the basic health needs of iran and  do we need  really a major center with all multi  specialty clinic and multi-speciality  or can we expand our money and have our  priority in the villages  which has the basic health problem upper  respiratory tract infection  in the winter and diarrhea in the summer  these are two major killer in  two seasons by only treating these  two major problems and  improving the nutritional status of the  children  we have certainly contributed a lot to  the health of  our population  [Music]  mrs borghar is one of 46 literate  villagers in  forest province who trained for six  months in a health center  [Music]  back in her village she makes home  visits to give advice on hygiene and  sanitation  [Music]  she also inspects water supplies  [Music]  [A